IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc8-sch2`

-- Tests for ssc8-sch2.l4 (Schedule 2). Expected values are worked by hand from the paragraph named beside each assertion.

§ `Tests for Schedule 2`

§§ `Builders (test helpers)`

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      relevant IS A BOOLEAN
      outside IS A BOOLEAN
      chargeable IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `sch 2 a profit`
`sch 2 test a profit` MEANS `sch 2 a profit` OF amount, relevant, outside, chargeable

GIVEN kind IS A `sch 2 para 3(5) kind of payment`
      amount IS A NUMBER
      chargeable IS A NUMBER
      relief IS A BOOLEAN
      wholly IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `sch 2 para 3(5) a payment`
`sch 2 test a payment` MEANS `sch 2 para 3(5) a payment` OF kind, amount, chargeable, relief, wholly

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      immediate IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `sch 2 para 4 a share`
`sch 2 test a share` MEANS `sch 2 para 4 a share` OF amount, immediate

§§ `Paragraph 1 -- interpretation`

#ASSERT `sch 2 para 1 the meaning of the term` `sch 2 para 1 the Act of 1988` EQUALS JUST "the Income and Corporation Taxes Act 1988"
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 1 the meaning of the term` `sch 2 para 1 ITTOIA 2005` EQUALS JUST "the Income Tax (Trading and Other Income) Act 2005"
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 1 the meaning of the term` `sch 2 para 1 ITA 2007` EQUALS JUST "the Income Tax Act 2007"
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 1 the meaning of the term` `sch 2 para 1 year` EQUALS JUST "year of assessment within the meaning of the Income Tax Acts (see section 989 of ITA 2007)"
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 1 the meaning of the term` `sch 2 para 1 some other term` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 2 -- the profits on which Class 4 contributions are payable`

-- both limbs met: payable.
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 2 the profit is one in respect of which Class 4 contributions are payable` (`sch 2 test a profit` 1000 TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not a profit of a relevant trade, profession or vocation; carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom; not chargeable under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of ITTOIA 2005: the paragraph says nothing.
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 2 the profit is one in respect of which Class 4 contributions are payable` (`sch 2 test a profit` 1000 FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 2 the profit is one in respect of which Class 4 contributions are payable` (`sch 2 test a profit` 1000 TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 2 the profit is one in respect of which Class 4 contributions are payable` (`sch 2 test a profit` 1000 TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the full amount: 1000 + 300 count; 500 (wholly outside) and 200 (not chargeable) do not.
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 2 the full amount of the profits in respect of which Class 4 contributions are payable` (LIST (`sch 2 test a profit` 1000 TRUE FALSE TRUE), (`sch 2 test a profit` 500 TRUE TRUE TRUE), (`sch 2 test a profit` 300 TRUE FALSE TRUE), (`sch 2 test a profit` 200 TRUE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS 1300
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 2 the full amount of the profits in respect of which Class 4 contributions are payable` EMPTY EQUALS 0

§§ `Paragraph 3(1) and (2) -- reliefs`

#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(1) relief is available under the provision` `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 sections 64 and 72` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "but only where loss arises from activities the profits ... of which would be brought into computation": otherwise no.
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(1) relief is available under the provision` `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 sections 64 and 72` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(1) relief is available under the provision` `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 section 83` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(1) relief is available under the provision` `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 section 83` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(1) relief is available under the provision` `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 section 89` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- provisions that sub-paragraph (1) does not list: not covered (the list is not closed).
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(1) relief is available under the provision` `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 section 383` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(1) relief is available under the provision` `sch 2 para 3 section 639` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(1) relief is available under the provision` `sch 2 para 3 some other provision` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(2) the relief provision does not apply` `sch 2 para 3 Act of 1988 Chapter I of Part VII` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(2) the relief provision does not apply` `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 Chapters 2 and 3 of Part 3` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(2) the relief provision does not apply` `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 sections 457, 458 and 459` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(2) the relief provision does not apply` `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 section 383` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(2) the relief provision does not apply` `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 sections 88 and 94` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(2) the relief provision does not apply` `sch 2 para 3 sections 619 and 620` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(2) the relief provision does not apply` `sch 2 para 3 section 639` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the provisions of sub-paragraph (1) are not named in (2): not covered by (2).
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(2) the relief provision does not apply` `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 sections 64 and 72` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(2) the relief provision does not apply` `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 section 83` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(2) the relief provision does not apply` `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 section 89` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(2) the relief provision does not apply` `sch 2 para 3 some other provision` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 3(4) -- a loss deducted and carried forward`

-- deduction 1000 against profits 400, 300, 500, 800: year 1 absorbs 400 (carry 600), year 2 absorbs 300 (carry 300), year 3 absorbs 300 (leaving 200), year 4 is untouched.
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(4) the profits for each year after the loss is deducted` TRUE (`Tax year` OF 1995) 1000 (LIST 400, 300, 500, 800) EQUALS JUST (LIST 0, 0, 200, 800)
-- a deduction larger than all the profits given leaves the rest to carry on: 5000 - 400 - 300 = 4300.
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(4) the profits for each year after the loss is deducted` TRUE (`Tax year` OF 1995) 5000 (LIST 400, 300) EQUALS JUST (LIST 0, 0)
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(4) the excess still to be deducted after the last year given` 5000 (LIST 400, 300) EQUALS 4300
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(4) the excess still to be deducted after the last year given` 1000 (LIST 400, 300, 500, 800) EQUALS 0
-- "as far as may be": a year with no profits absorbs nothing (-100 stays -100, the 50 carries to year 2, leaving 300 - 50 = 250).
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(4) the profits for each year after the loss is deducted` TRUE (`Tax year` OF 1995) 50 (LIST (-100), 300) EQUALS JUST (LIST (-100), 250)
-- boundaries of the year: 1990-91 is the first year; 1989-90 is before it.
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(4) the profits for each year after the loss is deducted` TRUE (`Tax year` OF 1990) 100 (LIST 400) EQUALS JUST (LIST 300)
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(4) the profits for each year after the loss is deducted` TRUE (`Tax year` OF 1989) 100 (LIST 400) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the person does not claim and is not allowed relief: not covered.
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(4) the profits for each year after the loss is deducted` FALSE (`Tax year` OF 1995) 100 (LIST 400) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 3(5) -- payments relieved`

-- (b) a section 383 payment for which relief from income tax can be given, incurred wholly for the trade: the whole 200.
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(5) the amount of the payment for which relief is allowed` (`sch 2 test a payment` `sch 2 para 3(5)(b) a payment under section 383 of ITA 2007` 200 0 TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST 200
-- no income tax relief is or can be given for it: not covered.
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(5) the amount of the payment for which relief is allowed` (`sch 2 test a payment` `sch 2 para 3(5)(b) a payment under section 383 of ITA 2007` 200 0 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (c) a payment with tax deducted under section 900(2), 903(5) or 906(5): 150.
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(5) the amount of the payment for which relief is allowed` (`sch 2 test a payment` `sch 2 para 3(5)(c) a payment from which tax must be deducted under section 900(2), 903(5) or 906(5) of ITA 2007` 150 0 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST 150
-- (d) only so much of the payment as equals "the chargeable amount": 80 of 300.
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(5) the amount of the payment for which relief is allowed` (`sch 2 test a payment` `sch 2 para 3(5)(d) a payment from which tax must be deducted under section 910(2) of ITA 2007` 300 80 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST 80
-- (e) a payment under a direction under section 944(2): 60.
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(5) the amount of the payment for which relief is allowed` (`sch 2 test a payment` `sch 2 para 3(5)(e) a payment from which tax must be deducted as a result of a direction under section 944(2) of ITA 2007` 60 0 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST 60
-- "so far as the payment is incurred wholly or exclusively for the purposes of any relevant trade": a payment not so incurred is outside the limit.
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(5) the amount of the payment for which relief is allowed` (`sch 2 test a payment` `sch 2 para 3(5)(c) a payment from which tax must be deducted under section 900(2), 903(5) or 906(5) of ITA 2007` 150 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a payment of a kind sub-paragraph (5) does not list: not covered.
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(5) the amount of the payment for which relief is allowed` (`sch 2 test a payment` `sch 2 para 3(5) some other payment` 99 0 TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Payments of 400, 300, 0, 50 against profits 1000, 100, 500, 700: year 1 absorbs 400 (600 left); year 2 can absorb only 100 (0 left, 200 carried);
-- year 3 absorbs the 200 (300 left); year 4 absorbs 50 (650 left).
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(5) the profits for each year after the payments are deducted` (LIST (`sch 2 para 3 a year` OF 1000, 400), (`sch 2 para 3 a year` OF 100, 300), (`sch 2 para 3 a year` OF 500, 0), (`sch 2 para 3 a year` OF 700, 50)) EQUALS LIST 600, 0, 300, 650
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(5) the payments still to be deducted after the last year given` (LIST (`sch 2 para 3 a year` OF 1000, 400), (`sch 2 para 3 a year` OF 100, 300), (`sch 2 para 3 a year` OF 500, 0), (`sch 2 para 3 a year` OF 700, 50)) EQUALS 0
-- Payments of 500 against profits 100 then 50 (payments of nil in year 2): 100 absorbed in year 1 (400 carried), 50 in year 2 (350 carried).
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(5) the profits for each year after the payments are deducted` (LIST (`sch 2 para 3 a year` OF 100, 500), (`sch 2 para 3 a year` OF 50, 0)) EQUALS LIST 0, 0
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(5) the payments still to be deducted after the last year given` (LIST (`sch 2 para 3 a year` OF 100, 500), (`sch 2 para 3 a year` OF 50, 0)) EQUALS 350
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 3(5) the profits for each year after the payments are deducted` EMPTY EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `Paragraph 4 -- partnerships`

-- shares 500 and 200 are immediately derived (aggregated: 700); the 100 is not.
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 4(1) the profits in respect of which the partner's liability arises` TRUE (LIST (`sch 2 test a share` 500 TRUE), (`sch 2 test a share` 200 TRUE), (`sch 2 test a share` 100 FALSE)) EQUALS JUST 700
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 4(1) the profits in respect of which the partner's liability arises` TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST 0
-- not carried on jointly: sub-paragraph (1) says nothing.
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 4(1) the profits in respect of which the partner's liability arises` FALSE (LIST (`sch 2 test a share` 500 TRUE)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 4(2) the contributions are charged on the partner separately` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 4(2) the contributions are charged on the partner separately` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 5 -- trustees, etc.`

#ASSERT `sch 2 para 5 Class 4 contributions are payable on the profits received as trustee` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 5 Class 4 contributions are payable on the profits received as trustee` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 6 -- other provisions`

#ASSERT `sch 2 para 6(1) section 101 of the Finance Act 2009 applies to the sum` `sch 2 para 6(1) an amount due in respect of Class 4 contributions` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 6(1) section 101 of the Finance Act 2009 applies to the sum` `sch 2 para 6(1) a sum to be paid by Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs in respect of Class 4 contributions` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 6(1) section 101 of the Finance Act 2009 applies to the sum` `sch 2 para 6(1) some other sum` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 6(1) section 102 of the Finance Act 2009 applies to the sum` `sch 2 para 6(1) a sum to be paid by Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs in respect of Class 4 contributions` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 6(1) section 102 of the Finance Act 2009 applies to the sum` `sch 2 para 6(1) an amount due in respect of Class 4 contributions` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 6(1) section 102 of the Finance Act 2009 applies to the sum` `sch 2 para 6(1) some other sum` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 7 -- final assessments`

#ASSERT `sch 2 para 7 the assessment is final and conclusive for computing Class 4 liability` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 7 the assessment is final and conclusive for computing Class 4 liability` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- neither exception: the bar stands.
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 7 the allowance or adjustment may be taken into account in computing the profits` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- either exception (or both): the bar ends; the sentence does not itself grant the allowance.
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 7 the allowance or adjustment may be taken into account in computing the profits` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 7 the allowance or adjustment may be taken into account in computing the profits` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 7 the allowance or adjustment may be taken into account in computing the profits` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 8 -- appeals`

#ASSERT `sch 2 para 8 Part V of the Taxes Management Act 1970 applies to the matter` `sch 2 para 8 an appeal or other matter under Part V of the Taxes Management Act 1970 in relation to Class 4 contributions` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 8 Part V of the Taxes Management Act 1970 applies to the matter` `sch 2 para 8 a decision under section 17(1) whether a person is excepted from liability for Class 4 contributions or the liability is deferred` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 8 Part V of the Taxes Management Act 1970 applies to the matter` `sch 2 para 8 a decision under regulations made by virtue of section 17(3) or (4) or 18` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 2 para 8 Part V of the Taxes Management Act 1970 applies to the matter` `sch 2 para 8 some other matter` EQUALS NOTHING
